&lt;p&gt;# Comments: 0&lt;/p&gt;</description><guid isPermaLink="false">https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=50071696</guid><pubDate>Tue, 13 Oct 2026 13:46:10 +0000</pubDate></item><item><title>Show HN: Mana – family organizer with an AI assistant</title><link>https://ourmana.app/</link><description>&lt;p&gt;Hi HN, I built Mana, a family organizer: shared calendars, shopping lists, receipt scanners, meal planning, chores, and notes for the whole household, with a built-in AI assistant ("add milk and eggs," "plan dinners for the week") plus automations (e.g., milk goes back on the list before it runs out).&lt;p&gt;Additionally, you can connect Mana MCP to your Claude, ChatGPT, Gemini etc.&lt;p&gt;The goal is to eventually take the model calls and storage to local but that's work to be done.&lt;p&gt;Appreciate if there's any feedback. Thank you!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr /&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Comments URL: &lt;a href="https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=50071636"&gt;https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=50071636&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Points: 1&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;# Comments: 0&lt;/p&gt;</description><guid isPermaLink="false">https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=50071636</guid><pubDate>Tue, 13 Oct 2026 13:42:05 +0000</pubDate></item><item><title>Show HN: I found a new planetary candidate in Kepler Data with AI</title><link>https://kuber.studio/planethunt/</link><description>&lt;p&gt;Hey HN! I was playing around with the Kepler and TESS data last weekend when I hacked around a way to pixel-peep stars dimming periodically to potentially find new exoplanets with Codex.&lt;p&gt;I ended up running the engine to find an interesting signal in Kepler data that was uncatalogued with a dip repeating every 13.77 days around KIC 5689121, a red dwarf in Lyra about 970 light-years away. If it's a planet, it'd be roughly 2.5–3 times Earth's radius !&lt;p&gt;Funnily enough, this candidate is just 7.1 arcseconds from a much brighter neighbour (KIC 5689116) and is very hard to see because of how much brighter it is (probably why it went unnoticed for so long)&lt;p&gt;Of course, there's work to do before calling it confirmed - my TRICERATOPS analysis is about 6.9% and we have to get IR/AO / Keck observations to prove it's out there ! (which I'm honestly intimidated by but cautiously optimistic about because I've never worked in non-CS adjacent research) but I found the activity of making cool tools to potentially discover things about our universe quite fun !&lt;p&gt;Would love feedback, especially from anyone who's worked with Kepler data or exoplanet validation :)&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://x.com/kuberwastaken/status/2109240782368751834" rel="nofollow"&gt;https://x.com/kuberwastaken/status/2109240782368751834&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr /&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Comments URL: &lt;a href="https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=50071497"&gt;https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=50071497&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
